{"name":"Amazon Jungle","hex":"#686747","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"amazon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tall, strong, athletic woman.","A fairy chess piece which combines the moves of the queen and the knight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amazon"},{"term":"jungle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, lush, undeveloped, humid forest, especially in a tropical region, thick with vegetation and wildlife; a tropical  rainforest.","Any uncultivated tract of forest or scrub habitat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["(Of musical beat, rhythm, etc.) resembling the fast-paced drumming of traditional peoples of the jungle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jungle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Amazon rainforest","blocks":[{"text":"The Amazon rainforest, also called the Amazon jungle, Amazonia, or simply the Amazon, is a moist broadleaf tropical rainforest in the Amazon biome that covers most of the Amazon basin of South America. This basin encompasses 7 million km2 (2.7 million sq mi), of which 6 million km2 (2.3 million sq mi) are covered by the rainforest. This region includes territory belonging to nine nations and 3,344 indigenous territories."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Amazon17_%285641020319%29.jpg/330px-Amazon17_%285641020319%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_rainforest"},{"title":"Amazon (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Amazon.com, Inc. is an American multinational conglomerate engaged in e-commerce, retail, cloud computing, online advertising, digital streaming, entertainment, and artificial intelligence. Founded in 1994 by Jeff Bezos in Bellevue, Washington, the company started as an online book marketplace that gradually expanded to include virtually all consumer products as well as many other categories, positioned as \"The Everything Store\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Amazon_Tower_I_topped_out%2C_June_2015.jpg/330px-Amazon_Tower_I_topped_out%2C_June_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_(company)"},{"title":"Jungle","blocks":[{"text":"A jungle is an area of land covered with dense forest and tangled vegetation, usually in tropical climates. Application of the term has varied greatly during the past century. Because jungles occur on all inhabited landmasses and may incorporate numerous vegetation and land types in different climatic zones, the wildlife of jungles cannot be straightforwardly defined."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/%E1%9E%96%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9F%83%E1%9E%80%E1%9E%98%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%96%E1%9E%BB%E1%9E%87%E1%9E%B6.jpg/330px-%E1%9E%96%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9F%83%E1%9E%80%E1%9E%98%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%96%E1%9E%BB%E1%9E%87%E1%9E%B6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle"},{"title":"Jungle green","blocks":[{"text":"Jungle green is a color that is a rich tone of medium spring green."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle_green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Naturalist_on_the_River_Amazons_figure_4.png/500px-Naturalist_on_the_River_Amazons_figure_4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Naturalist_on_the_River_Amazons_figure_4.png/1280px-Naturalist_on_the_River_Amazons_figure_4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Naturalist_on_the_River_Amazons_figure_4.png/500px-Naturalist_on_the_River_Amazons_figure_4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bates's 1863 The Natura